OL,5,CTRAIN CRASHFin Staffordshire:
OL,6, Fone dead, more than 50 hurt...103B203
OL,8,CSOUTH AFRICAFHowe meets Tambo
OL,9,F for talks in London...........113B213
OL,10,FUp to five killed in Soweto....114B214
OL,12,CSTOCKHOLMFNo agreement likely
OL,13,F today at security conference..106B206
OL,15,CUSA-USSRFexploratory summit
OL,16,F talks continue................104B204
OL,17,FDaniloff case "being used".....105B205
OL,19,CN IRELANDFBomb attacks on
OL,20,F Catholic homes................111B211
OL,22,T]CFThis Ceefax page is fromC20-09-86
OL,23,T]CFMuch more at: teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11804
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789942524
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A train driver died and more than 50
OL,6, people were injured when two trains
OL,7, collided in Staffordshire yesterday.
OL,9,FThe dead man was Mr E Goode from Crewe,
OL,10,Faged in his fifties. Four people are
OL,11,Fcritically or seriously ill and being
OL,12,Fthreated in an intensive care unit.
OL,14,FBR said the 17.00 Euston-Manchester and
OL,15,Fthe 17.20 Liverpool-Euston struck one
OL,16,Fanother a glancing blow at Colwick
OL,17,FJunction then derailed.
OL,19,FThe southbound train was travelling at
OL,20,F90-100mph, the other at 50-60mph. BR
OL,21,Fhas begun an internal ingestigation.
OL,23,T]CFrom 20-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789942524
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, The general manager of British Rail's
OL,6, London-Midland Region said about 800
OL,7, people were on the two trains which
OL,8, collided at Colwich Junction.
OL,10,FMr Cyril Bleasdale said more would have
OL,11,Fbeen injured if the carriages had not
OL,12,Fbeen relatively modern.
OL,14,FHe said he understood both trains were
OL,15,Fon time and that the train from
OL,16,FLiverpool should have cleared the
OL,17,Fjunction before the train from Euston.
OL,19,FModern electric-lighting signalling was
OL,20,Fused on the stretch of track and there
OL,21,Fwas a signal box about 60 yards from
OL,22,Fthe crash site, he added.
OL,23,                      D]CFrom 20-09-86
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789942524
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     GG6/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, The general manager of British Rail's
OL,6, London-Midland Region said a second man
OL,7, was travelling in the cab of one of the
OL,8, trains in yesterday's rail crash.
OL,10,FMr Cyril Bleasdale said the man was in
OL,11,Fthe cab of the Euston to Manchester
OL,12,Fexpress. He and the driver jumped from
OL,13,Fthe cab seconds before the collision.
OL,15,FThe man is understood to have been a
OL,16,FBR employee - in some cases they are
OL,17,Fauthorised to travel with the driver.
OL,19,FOf the 52 injured in the crash, 32 are
OL,20,Fstill in hospital.
OL,23,T]CFrom 20-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11807
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789942524
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Foreign Secretary Sir Geoffrey Howe has
OL,6, met the acting head of the exiled
OL,7, African National Congress in London.
OL,9,FA foreign office spokesman said Sir
OL,10,FGeoffrey and Mr Oliver Tambo had had
OL,11,Fa good, candid and open meeting.
OL,13,FThe two hours of talks centred on the
OL,14,Fcurrent situation in South Africa and
OL,15,Fprospects for a peaceful settlement
OL,16,Fthere, the spokesman said.
OL,18,FSir Geoffrey emphasised Britain's
OL,19,Fopposition to apartheid and its wish
OL,20,Fto see rapid, fundamental but peaceful
OL,21,Fchange.
OL,23,T]CFrom 20-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11808
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789942524
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Reports from South Africa say up to
OL,6, five people have been shot dead in an
OL,7, incident in the township of Soweto.
OL,9,FThe Bureau for Information said a 24-
OL,10,Fyear-old woman was killed when police
OL,11,Fopened fire on a crowd which was
OL,12,Fstoning passing cars.
OL,14,FLocal residents said between two and
OL,15,Ffive people were killed and another 12
OL,16,Finjured in violence during a night
OL,17,Fvigil for a murder victim.
OL,19,FPolice action went far beyond that
OL,20,Fdescribed in the official account, they
OL,21,Fsaid.
OL,23,T]CFrom 20-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11809
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789942524
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, No effective agreement is expected to
OL,6, be reached today at the Stockholm arms
OL,7, control conference.
OL,9,FDelegates "stopped the clock" at the
OL,10,Fconference so they could continue talks
OL,11,Ftoday without breaching the midnight
OL,12,Fdeadline for the 32-month negotiations.
OL,13,         F
OL,14,FObservers now believe that an agreement
OL,15,Fis more likely on Monday.
OL,17,FThe conference is attempting to devise
OL,18,Fa formula whereby major troop movements
OL,19,Fin Europe would be announced in advance
OL,20,Fand on-site inspections of military
OL,21,Fformations would be allowed.
OL,23,T]CFrom 20-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11810
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789942524
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G10/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, US-Soviet talks on a possible summit
OL,6, have resumed in Washington, with the
OL,7, Daniloff affair still casting a shadow
OL,8, over the proceedings.
OL,10,FYesterday President Reagan had an
OL,11,Funscheduled meeting with Soviet foreign
OL,12,Fminister Mr Eduard Shevardnadze.
OL,14,FToday Mr Shevardnadze continued talks
OL,15,Fwith US Secretary of State Mr George
OL,16,FShultz.
OL,18,FThey are said to be working on a four-
OL,19,Fpoint summit agenda, consisting of arms
OL,20,Fcontrol, regional issues, humanitarian
OL,21,Fquestions and bilateral affiars.
OL,23,T]CFrom 20-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11811
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789942524
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G11/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Soviet Communist Party newspaper
OL,6, Pravda says the US is using Nicholas
OL,7, Daniloff's arrest to frustrate a new
OL,8, superpower summit.
OL,10,FPravda echoed Soviet leader Mr Mikhail
OL,11,FGorbachev in calling journalist
OL,12,FNicholas Daniloff a spy and said there
OL,13,Fhad been an "escalation of anti-
OL,14,FSovietism" over the affair.
OL,16,FThis, the paper said, was part of a
OL,17,Fpattern of behaviour by the US "to
OL,18,Ffrustrate a possible summit and pass
OL,19,Fthe blame for it onto Moscow".
OL,23,T]CFrom 20-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11812
